    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d550">

                <pb facs="0497" n="381" xml:id="pg381"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 738.3915/96.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to
                            Haiti to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1019.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 8, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith copy
                    and translation of a note of the Dominican Legation to the Haitian Government
                    relative to the boundary question.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d550-f1"/> The copy was
                    furnished me by the Dominican Legation. Since its receipt I have had several
                    informal talks on the subject with Minister Henriquez and Secretary Léger. I
                    have tried to impress both parties with the necessity for prompt action looking
                    to the speedy settlement of the question rather than long discussions which
                    accomplish nothing. * * *</p>
                <p>I have [etc.],</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">H. W. Furniss.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d550-f1" n="1" xml:id="d550-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it discusses discrepancies between the maps, and the consequent
                    divergence of opinion relating to the status quo line.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
